Body:
Issue I noticed is the difference of how events are sent from the `/chat/completion` and the '/responses` api is.

```log
[chat-stream] text-start {
  "id": "txt-0"
}
[chat-stream] text-delta {
  "id": "txt-0",
  "text": "Hello"
}
[chat-stream] text-delta {
  "id": "txt-0",
  "text": "!"
}
```

```log
[stream] text-start {
  "id": ""
}
[stream] text-start {
  "id": ""
}
[stream] text-delta {
  "id": "",
  "text": "2"
}
[stream] text-start {
  "id": ""
}
[stream] text-delta {
  "id": "",
  "text": " +"
}
```

So I might make a change to accept the `text-delta` even before the `text-start`, or is it best I force `text-start` to come before `text-delta` from the provider sdk itself?

@johanwulf you can increase timeouts if you need to doing the following (timeout is in ms):
```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "openai": {
      "options": {
        "timeout": 600000
      }
    }
  }
}
```

this is just latency from your provider, not opencode's fault 

